/*World types:
D1 always starts from left and D2 always starts from right.
1-10: Highway Code Agents
101-110: Questionnaire - No Communication Agents
201-210: Questionnaire - Communicative Agents
301-310: Questionnaire - Higher Order Negotiation Agents

Scenarios are shared across the different types of agents.


1-4: 2 drivers.
    1: PP in middle to left of d1. (Q4 Scenario)
    2: PP behind to left of d1.
    3: PP behind to right of d1. (Q5 Scenario)
    4: PP behind to left of d1 AND PP behind to the right of d2.
5-8: 3 drivers.
    5: PP in middle to left of d1, extra car behind d2.
    6: PP in middle to right of d1, extra car behind d2. (Q7 Scenario)
    7: PP behind to left of d1, extra car behind d1. (Q9 Scenario)
    8: PP in middle to the left of d1 AND behind to the left of d1 AND behind to the left of d2, extra car behind d1.
9-10: 4 drivers.
    9: PP in middle to right of d1. 3 drivers on each side(Q8 Scenario)
    10: PP in middle to right of d1 AND behind to the left of d1 AND behind to the left of d6. 3 drivers on each side.


Questionnaire agents - no communication
101-104: 2 driverq_nocomm agents.
105-108: 3 driverq_nocomm agents.
109-110: 4 driverq_nocomm agents.

Questionnaire agents - primitive communication
201-204: 2 driverq_comm agents.
205-208: 3 driverq_comm agents.
209-210: 4 driverq_comm agents.

Questionnaire agents - higher order negotiation
301-304: 2 driverq_hon agents.
305-308: 3 driverq_hon agents.
309-310: 4 driverq_hon agents.
*/


/*
To change scenarios:
-Type in the desired environment and number of agents based on the above into example.Env(*Environment number*, *Number of agents*)
-Uncomment the agent type for the scenario, comment out the rest
-Edit the number of agents after the # to match the number input into the environment.
*/
MAS main {

    //(world option number, number of agents)
    environment: example.Env(1,2)

    agents: driverhc #1;
            //driverq_nocomm #3;
            //driverq_comm #3;
            //driverq_hon #4;

    aslSourcePath: "src/agt";
}
